<title>USA: Harris Corp wins contracts worth $17 mln.</title>
<headline>Harris Corp wins contracts worth $17 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE, Fla. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harris Corp said on Wednesday it was awarded three communications-services contracts worth a total of $17 million.</p>
<p>The contracts include an $8 million deal with Valero Natural Gas Partners LP ; a $6.5 million deal with the city of Dallas and a $2.5 million deal with the Rhode Island state police.</p>
<p>All the contracts involve relocating communications networks from 2 GHz to 6 GHz, the company said.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
